From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ar <sm64ar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Capture hooks and draw tags

Adds the renderer side of the AR capture: a hook table (gGfxArHooks, NULL by
default, in src/pc/gfx/gfx_ar_hooks.h) and G_NOOP tag words ("AR" in the high
16 bits, then kind and argument) that the game emits into its display lists.

- gfx_pc: WORLD draws reach the capture backend in level space, without
  projection, aspect correction, clip reject, CPU backface culling or fog;
  the cull mode is reported instead. Rectangles stay SCREEN. The host can
  set the rotation used for light and texgen directions (the lighting
  camera), so models are lit from the viewer's head.
- the game (with gArMode) brackets camera-space nodes with WORLD tags, the 2D
  passes with overlay group tags (misc, counters, power meter, dialog,
  pause) and each player's own display lists with FOCUS tags
  for an x-ray silhouette; the background node draws neither skybox nor
  fill colour and frame/viewport clears emit nothing.

With gGfxArHooks == NULL and gArMode == false the renderer and the game
behave exactly like upstream.
